{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1477241","title":"The characteristics of prokaryotic microbial communities in receiving river water bodies of different cities","description":"In this study, we investigated prokaryotic microbial communities in three urban rivers with distinct water sources, including a natural river, a reclaimed water river, and an effluent river. Using 16S rRNA gene sequencing in combination with environmental factor analysis, co-occurrence network analysis, and community assembly models, we systematically characterized microbial diversity, community composition, ecological interactions, and assembly processes across the three rivers. Through the simultaneous comparison of both microbial domains, we aimed to elucidate how reclaimed water and effluent inputs reshape microbial communities and to identify the ecological mechanisms underlying community organization under different levels of anthropogenic disturbance. This study provides new insights into the ecological dynamics of urban river microbiomes and offers a scientific basis for evaluating the ecological consequences of water reuse and effluent discharge in freshwater ecosystems.","center":"Ningbo University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/06/10 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN60749049","Metagenome or environmental sample from freshwater metagenome","probable_urban","water_drainage",null,2023,"CN","Zhejiang",1799397,"Ningbo","verified",29.948,121.503,"China: Ningbo","river",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN60749050","Metagenome or environmental sample from freshwater metagenome","probable_urban","water_drainage",null,2023,"CN","Zhejiang",1799397,"Ningbo","verified",29.948,121.50